    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That \"Yo\" one is definitely much more casual. To be honest, we're trying to figure out if we should actually lean into specific dialects or slang for certain zip codes to really hit that \"authentic\" feel. If we were targeting a younger, more street-level demographic in those areas, how would you adjust the tone further? Like, give me something that sounds even more natural to that specific culture so they don't feel like we're just some corporate entity talking down to them.",
